.TH RFID-MODE-RUNNER 1 "2026-07-28" "GWAY local tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rfid-mode-runner \- run local modes selected by RFID card paths
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rfid-mode-runner
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rfid-mode-runner
watches the RFID scan JSON file and interprets
.I /home/arthe/.config/rfid-modes/cards
as a state machine. It starts, stops, and supervises command scripts created by
.BR rfid-register (1).
.PP
When a top-level card has both a directory and a sidecar command script, the
runner treats the sidecar as a one-shot action by default and keeps navigation
at the root. Add
.B RFID_MODE_STATEFUL=1
to the sidecar only when the card is intentionally a long-lived mode or selector
that should enter its own directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --scan-file " FILE"
Read scans from
.IR FILE .
.TP
.BI --config-dir " DIR"
Use a non-default RFID mode config directory.
.TP
.B --once
Process the current scan once and exit.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Log actions without starting or stopping scripts.
.TP
.B --status
Print the current runner state JSON.
.TP
.B --stop-current
Stop the currently running mode process.
.SH SCRIPT ENVIRONMENT
Started scripts receive variables such as
.BR RFID_MODE_CARD_ID ,
.BR RFID_MODE_SCANNED_AT ,
.BR RFID_MODE_SCAN_FILE ,
.BR RFID_MODE_KIND ,
.BR RFID_MODE_STATE_PATH ,
.BR RFID_MODE_HOLD ,
and
.BR RFID_MODE_NEW .
.PP
A transition script declaring
.B RFID_MODE_PREEMPT_ACTION=1
is first invoked with
.B RFID_MODE_PREEMPT_ONLY=1
before the runner stops a currently tracked mode. Exit status 0 consumes the
scan as a secondary action; exit status 75 continues to the script's normal
primary transition. Any other exit status safely consumes the scan without
switching the current mode.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
/home/arthe/.local/bin/rfid-mode-runner --status
/home/arthe/.local/bin/rfid-mode-runner --once --dry-run
/home/arthe/.local/bin/rfid-mode-runner --stop-current
systemctl --user status rfid-mode-runner.service --no-pager
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rfid-commands (1),
.BR rfid-register (1),
.BR rfid-scan-publisher (1)
